 "structure": "Single PDF 'Academic Standards for Geography' (Final Form Annex A, July 18 2002; 22 Pa. Code Ch.4 App. C). Front matter pp.1-4 (title, TOC, introduction incl. Five Fundamental Themes table). Four categories: 7.1 Basic Geographic Literacy (A Geographic Tools, B Location of Places and Regions), 7.2 Physical Characteristics of Places and Regions (A, B Physical Processes), 7.3 Human Characteristics (A Population, B Culture, C Settlement, D Economic Activity, E Political Activity), 7.4 Interactions Between People and Places (A Impact of Physical Systems on People, B Impact of People on Physical Systems). Each category: table with header 7.x.3 GRADE 3 / 7.x.6 GRADE 6 / 7.x.9 GRADE 9 / 7.x.12 GRADE 12 (C1-C4), a stem row, lettered statements with bullet (and nested) descriptors in the same cell, a closing note row about local-to-global progression. Tables continue across pages without headers (C1=Gr3, C2=Gr6, C3=Gr9, C4=Gr12). Loose x= fragments are scrambled duplicates of the cell text (x acts as vertical position). Rows: Gr3->K-3, Gr6->4-6, Gr9->7-9, Gr12->10-12. Glossary pp.14-24 (backup).",
